,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducable: v4.6.dev.custom_build [1e9d0ff92], v4.0.stable.official [92bee43ad]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev (1e9d0ff92) - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.5599) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 15.76 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nFound while investigating #105564, but smaller MRP provided.\n\nIf currently selecting a canvas item in the tree dock then clicking on a canvas item with visibility toggled off that is listed below the current selection in the tree dock, then the selection highlight for the first selection remains when no selection should be shown. \n\nIn the screen shot below, the selection is shown for the node \"Visible 1\" but only \"Hidden\" is selected.\n<img width=\"861\" height=\"481\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86a9cc89-45b1-47f6-b26f-bc31f8c81f11\" />\n\nBug does not occur if the positions in the tree dock are swapped. As in, first selecting a visible canvas item then selecting a non-visible canvas item listed above the first.\nBug also resolves itself if the cursor is moved into the scene viewport probably because that triggers a fresh redraw.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn the MRP:\n\n1. Open the \"hidden_selection\" scene\n2. Go into 2D mode\n3. Click the node \"Visible 1\" in the scene tree dock\n4. Click the node \"Hidden\" in the scene tree dock\n5. Notice how the selection is still around \"Visible 1\" in the scene view\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[select_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22933185/select_mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubu